`site.yaml` is the central configuration file for your Engobe site. This post covers all available options.

## Site Metadata

```yaml
title: My Engobe Site
description: A blazingly fast static site generator
baseUrl: https://example.com
language: en
theme: default
```

- `title`: Site name (used in templates)
- `description`: Meta description tag
- `baseUrl`: Full URL to your site
- `language`: Language code (for HTML lang attribute)
- `theme`: Theme directory name

## Public Asset URLs

`assetPrefix` is the public URL base for Engobe-owned assets. Physical files always remain under `_site/assets/`; the URL path is not an output directory. For example, `https://cdn.example.com/v2/media/` must map at the CDN origin to the contents of `_site/assets/`. Engobe does not upload assets or configure CDN caching.

```yaml
baseUrl: https://example.org/docs/
assetPrefix: /media/
```

Use `asset_url('css/site.css')`, `plugin_asset_url('search', 'js/index.js')`, and `page_asset_url('hero.jpg')` in themes. A root-relative prefix receives the base path once, while an absolute CDN prefix keeps its own origin and path. A `--base-url` override changes local asset URLs and the site origin used for feeds, not an absolute CDN base.

**BREAKING template behavior:** `site.asset_prefix` now exposes the effective public base, including the base path and exactly one trailing slash. A theme that previously used `site.base_path + site.asset_prefix` must remove that extra composition. `assetPrefix` is camelCase; there is no `asset_prefix` configuration alias.

Production projects owned `src`, `href`, `srcset`, and `poster` attributes, CSS `url()` and both `@import` forms, and the HTML content of Atom feeds. Feed asset URLs are absolute. Query strings and fragments are preserved. Inline CSS/scripts, arbitrary example text, and JavaScript imports are not rewritten. Pagefind stays under the site's local `/pagefind/` path; only Engobe's own search script uses the asset prefix.

Fingerprints use final asset bytes, with imported CSS finalized before its importer. A CSS dependency cycle fails a fingerprinted build; resolve the cycle or deliberately set `build.fingerprint: false`. Prefix projection still applies without fingerprints. Production link checking examines local output files offline and does not verify CDN reachability, CORS, or caching; use `build.linkCheck: false` to disable existence checks.

Development replaces an absolute CDN base with local `/assets/`, but preserves a root-relative custom prefix. Restart `engobe serve` after changing the prefix or effective base path. The local asset namespace cannot overlap generated pages, enabled Pagefind routes, or live reload.

## Collections

```yaml
collections:
  posts:
    directory: content/posts
    permalink: /blog/:slug/
    sort: date desc
    paginate: 10
    feed: true
    layout: post
    taxonomies:
      - tags
      - categories
  pages:
    directory: content/pages
    permalink: /:slug/
    sort: weight asc
    layout: page
```

- `directory`: Source directory
- `permalink`: URL pattern (`:slug`, `:date`, `:title`)
- `sort`: Field and direction (`date desc`, `weight asc`)
- `paginate`: Items per page (pagination enabled if >0)
- `feed`: Generate RSS feed?
- `layout`: Default template name
- `taxonomies`: Applied taxonomy types

## Taxonomies

```yaml
taxonomies:
  tags:
    permalink: /tags/:slug/
    paginate: 20
    layout: taxonomy
  categories:
    permalink: /categories/:slug/
    paginate: 10
    layout: taxonomy
```

- `permalink`: URL pattern for taxonomy pages
- `paginate`: Items per page
- `layout`: Template for category pages

## Menus

```yaml
menus:
  main:
    - title: Home
      ref: posts/
    - title: About
      ref: pages/about
    - title: External
      url: https://example.com
      external: true
```

- `title`: Display text
- `ref`: Link to collection/page
- `url`: External URL (sets `external: true`)

## Build Options

```yaml
build:
  outputDirectory: _site
  cleanBefore: true
  minifyHtml: false
  minifyCss: false
```

- `outputDirectory`: Where to generate the site
- `cleanBefore`: Remove old output before build?
- `minifyHtml`: Compress HTML output?
- `minifyCss`: Compress CSS files?

## Development

```yaml
dev:
  port: 5555
  watch: true
  liveReload: true
```

- `port`: Dev server port
- `watch`: Watch files for changes?
- `liveReload`: Auto-refresh browser?

## Advanced

```yaml
markdown:
  extensions:
    - strikethrough
    - tables
    - task-lists

feeds:
  - collection: posts
    permalink: /feed.xml
```

- `markdown.extensions`: Enable CommonMark extensions
- `feeds`: RSS feeds per collection

Full documentation at [Engobe](https://engobe.studio)

Understanding these options gives you full control over your Engobe site!
